{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\paperh16841\paperw11899\margl567\margr567\margt567\margb720\psz9{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue255;}{\fonttbl\f0\fcharset0\fnil Arial;\f1\fcharset0\fnil Arial;\f2\fcharset0\fnil Times New Roman;\f3\fcharset0\fnil Times New Roman;\f4\fcharset0\fnil Arial;\f5\fcharset0\fnil Times New Roman;\f6\fcharset0\fnil Times New Roman;\f7\fcharset0\fnil Times;}\pard\plain\sb56\tx90\tx1853{\plain\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 1\plain\tab\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 Opening of the meeting{\fs29\par}}\pard\plain\sb11\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 3GPP TSG RAN WG3 Chair Ms. Yin GAO (ZTE) opened the f2f meeting RAN WG3 #121bis on Monday October 9th, {\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 2023 at 9am.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 On behalf of the host, the Chinese Friends of 3GPP (CF3), RAN3 Vice-Chair Mr. Gen Cao (China Unicom) welcomed the {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 participants to Xiamen, China and explained organisational aspects of the meeting.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\sb1296\tx90\tx1853{\plain\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 2\plain\tab\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 Reminders{\fs29\par}}\pard\plain\sb1500\tx90\tx1853{\plain\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 2.1\plain\tab\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 IPR Declaration{\fs29\par}}\pard\plain\sb11\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 The attention of the delegates to the meeting of this Technical Specification Group was drawn to the fact that 3GPP {\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Individual Members have the obligation under the IPR Policies of their respective Organizational Partners to inform their {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 respective Organizational Partners of Essential IPRs they become aware of.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 The delegates were asked to take note that they were thereby invited:{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 to investigate whether their organization or any other organization owns IPRs which were, or were likely to become Essential {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 in respect of the work of 3GPP.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 to notify their respective Organizational Partners of all potential IPRs, e.g., for ETSI, by means of the IPR Information {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Statement and the Licensing declaration forms.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\sb1351\tx90\tx1853{\plain\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 2.2\plain\tab\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 Statement of Antitrust Compliance{\fs29\par}}\pard\plain\sb11\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 The attention of the delegates to the meeting was drawn to the fact that 3GPP activities were subject to all applicable {\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 antitrust and competition laws and that compliance with said laws was therefore required by any participant of the meeting, {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 including the Chairman and Vice-Chairmen and were invited to seek any clarification needed with their legal counsel. The {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 leadership would conduct the present meeting with impartiality and in the interests of 3GPP. Delegates were reminded that {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 timely submission of work items in advance of TSG/WG meetings was important to allow for full and fair consideration of {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 such matters.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\sb1304\tx90\tx1853{\plain\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 2.3\plain\tab\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 Responsible IT Behavior{\fs29\par}}\pard\plain\sb11\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Delegates were reminded of the fair network use rules established by the PCG:{\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 1. Users shall not use the network to engage in illegal activities. This includes activities such as copyright violation, hacking, {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 espionage or any other activity that may be prohibited by local laws.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 2. Users shall not engage in non-work related activities that are consume excessive bandwidth or cause significant {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx566{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 degradation of the performance of the network.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\sb1312\tx90\tx1853{\plain\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 2.4\plain\tab\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 Additional reminders{\fs29\par}}{\page}\pard\plain\sb1246\tx90\tx1853{\plain\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 3\plain\tab\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 Approval of the Agenda{\fs29\par}}\pard\plain\sb254\tx90\tx1868\tqr\tx10648{\plain\fs20\b\f3\cf2\cb1 R3-235001\plain\tab\fs20\b\f7\cf0\cb1 RAN3#121-bis Meeting Agenda\plain\tab\fs20\i\b\f6\cf0\cb1 RAN3 Chair{\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\tx90{\plain\fs16\f4\cf0\cb1 Replaces {\fs21\par}}\pard\plain\sb399\tqr\tx10649{\plain\tab\fs20\ul\f5\cf0\cb1 The document was approved.{\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\sb39\tqr\tx10652{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Replaced by {\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\sb109\tx90\tx1853{\plain\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 4\plain\tab\fs24\b\f1\cf0\cb1 Approval of the minutes from previous meetings{\fs29\par}}\pard\plain\sb254\tx90\tx1868\tqr\tx10648{\plain\fs20\b\f3\cf2\cb1 R3-235002\plain\tab\fs20\b\f7\cf0\cb1 Draft RAN3#121 Meeting Report\plain\tab\fs20\i\b\f6\cf0\cb1 ETSI-MCC{\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\tx90{\plain\fs16\f4\cf0\cb1 Replaces {\fs21\par}}\pard\plain\sb115\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 no comments{\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\sb44\tqr\tx10649{\plain\tab\fs20\ul\f5\cf0\cb1 The document was revised.{\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\sb39\tqr\tx10652{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Replaced by R