qr\tx10649{\plain\tab\fs20\ul\f5\cf0\cb1 The document was noted.{\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\sb39\tqr\tx10652{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Replaced by {\fs25\par}}{\page}\pard\plain\tx90\tx1868\tqr\tx10648{\plain\fs20\b\f3\cf2\cb1 R3-235341\plain\tab\fs20\b\f7\cf0\cb1 (TP for L1L2Mob BLCR for TS 38.401): Discussion on LTM \plain\tab\fs20\i\b\f6\cf0\cb1 Huawei{\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\tx1868{\plain\tab\fs20\b\f7\cf0\cb1 procedures{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\sb21\tx90{\plain\fs16\f4\cf0\cb1 Replaces {\fs21\par}}\pard\plain\sb115\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 1: 	The LTM reference configuration contains two parts: the gNB-DU part (i.e. the Cell group {\fs25\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 configuration) and the gNB-CU part (i.e. the radio bearer configuration and the measurement configuration).9{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 2:	 The gNB-CU needs to explicitly request the candidate gNB-DU or source gNB-DU to provide {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 reference configuration via UE Context Setup Request message or UE Context Modification Request message in case{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1  the reference configuration is a complete configuration for LTM. {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 3:	 The gNB-CU provides the reference configuration to all other candidate gNB-DUs via UE Context {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Modification Request message.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 4:	 The candidate DUs responds the delta configuration to the gNB-CU in the response message.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 5:	 No need for the gNB-CU to request the candidate gNB-DU to provide the RS configuration.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 6:	 No need for the gNB-CU to request gNB-DU to provide the TCI state configuration.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 7:	 A new class 2 procedure with the same name is used for transferring the selected beam information {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 from the gNB-CU to the target gNB-DU, i.e. LTM Cell Change Notification.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 8:	 Turn the following into agreement:{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 -	The CFRA resources are shared only among the UEs in a single gNB-DU to avoid the RACH access conflict {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 between UEs from different DU. {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 -	The gNB-CU indicates the source gNB-DU ID to the candidate DU when it requests the CFRA resources.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 -	To introduce 2 new class 2 non-UE associated F1 signalings to deliver the TA information from the candidate {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 gNB-DU to the source gNB-DU via gNB-CU.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 9:	 The following information together with the TA value is sent from the candidate gNB-DU to the source {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 gNB-DU: {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 -	detected RAP ID{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 -	source gNB-DU ID{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 -	candidate cell ID{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 -	RO information{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 -	carrier information{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 Proposal 10: 	The source gNB-DU transfers the TA information of candidate cells to the target gNB-DU after LTM {\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\cf0\cb1 cell switch for subsequent LTM.{\fs22\par}}\pard\plain\tx1190{\plain\tab\fs20\f2\